/* How much training history to keep.

   Measured, not guessed: a typical logged session (7 exercises, 3–5 sets each) serialises to ~1,095
   characters; a heavy one (12 exercises) to ~1,695. Everything else in the store — programs, gyms,
   notes, setup, bodyweight log, measurements — comes to roughly 23 KB combined, which is noise by
   comparison. localStorage gives about 5 MB per origin and stores strings as UTF-16, so the real
   budget is ~2.5 million CHARACTERS, not 5 million.

   That's why a plain count is the wrong instrument. At 2,000 sessions a typical user needs 2.19M
   chars and a heavy user 3.39M — the same number is simultaneously generous for one and over quota
   for the other. So the count is a ceiling and the BYTE budget is the real bound: 1.6M chars for
   history leaves ~36% of the quota free for the rest of the store, the in-progress session snapshot
   (wpb:live), and the corrupt-store backup that can transiently double usage.

   In practice that's roughly 1,460 sessions for a typical lifter and ~940 for someone logging huge
   full-body days — 5.6 and 3.6 years at five sessions a week, against 1.9 years under the old flat
   500. Trimming is still oldest-first, and the merge path reports anything it had to drop. */
